- B-V (color index): Giants often have higher B-V (redder) than dwarfs of same spectral type, but depends on spectral class.  
- SpType (spectral type): The luminosity class in spectral type (e.g., III for giants, V for main sequence) is a direct indicator of giant status.  
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Giants are more luminous (lower Amag values) than dwarfs; however, the given Amag values seem large and possibly inverted or in some transformed scale, so direct comparison is uncertain.  

